{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_k5BSkeSFuoxt1uVA2ghDlsbF","content":"1\tCreated-Local: 2026-11-03 08:0x +0700\n2\tCoding-Agent: kimi\n3\tSession: fresh (engineer round — routed here after muse (wedge) and agy-flash (wedge) on shiva)\n4\tWorktree: /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-xlang (branch feat/xlang-matrix @ ab3839b5 + uncommitted partial work)\n5\t\n6\t# Task: complete and gate xlang slice 1 — the shared conformance helper + the rebuilt cross_lang_test\n7\t\n8\t## State\n9\t\n10\t- test/yang/call/conformance.clj — NEW (uncommitted, ~9 KB), the shared helper from an interrupted muse round. Its docstring states the design: donor programs published as ordinary linker modules and run unmodified under their own entry; named exports read from the donor runtime global namespace and projected into the caller runtime namespace as nodes evaluated in the caller task (task-local cells, section 8.11); linked runs on the three vector VMs over the TypeScript linked harness content store; no call-node rewriting, no foreign :code extraction, no language-pair wrappers (yang.antlr.md section 8.10.11).\n11\t- test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj — REBUILT (+31/-136): the three tests (ts-closure-called-from-php, php-closure-called-from-ts, limits) re-expressed through the helper.\n12\t\n13\t## Measured gate failure (shiva, the previous gate run)\n14\t\n15\tyang.cross-lang-test JVM: 3 tests / 5 assertions / 2 failures / 1 error. Visible failure: the PHP->TS direction — (xl/call [:php src] [\"phpfn\"] [:typescript \"const n = phpfn(); ...\"]) expected js{:out [\"false false\"]} but got js{:out [], :uncaught \"TypeError: value is not a function\"} — the donor export does NOT reach the caller namespace as a callable.\n16\t\n17\t## Your job\n18\t\n19\t1. Read both files completely plus the harnesses they borrow from (test/yang/typescript/antlr/source_call_test.cljc, the php linked-profile tests) — the working composition pattern already exists there.\n20\t2. Complete/fix the helper and test