{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_41HwkQej3vWG9HQGzkZYWnZ6","content":"1\t(ns yang.cross-lang-test\n2\t  \"The substrate claim, empirically (yang.antlr.md 8.10/8.11): both preludes\n3\t   bottom out in `:application`, and the engine neither knows nor cares which\n4\t   frontend minted a closure. A TypeScript function value is called from\n5\t   PHP-lowered code and a PHP closure from TypeScript-lowered code, in one\n6\t   task, one run.\n7\t\n8\t   The seam is explicit published-export composition (8.10.11), owned by\n9\t   `yang.call.conformance`: the donor source is published as a module and\n10\t   run unmodified, its named export is read from the donor runtime's global\n11\t   namespace (`globalThis.ts_fn`, `$phpfn`) and projected into the caller\n12\t   runtime's namespace under the same name, and the caller source runs\n13\t   unmodified. No call node is rewritten and no foreign `:code` extracted:\n14\t   the caller holds the donor's own function cell, as the identity check\n15\t   (`stored === phpfn`) shows.\n16\t\n17\t   What is pinned as LIMITS (documented expectations, not failures):\n18\t   a PHP array reaching TypeScript is an opaque handle that only PHP can use;\n19\t   PHP null (`:php/null`) is neither JS null nor undefined. Each case runs\n20\t   linked on the three vector VMs, which must agree.\"\n21\t  (:require\n22\t    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n23\t    [yang.call.conformance :as xl]))\n24\t\n25\t\n26\t(deftest ts-closure-called-from-php-test\n27\t  (testing \"a number crosses as a number: float in, float out\"\n28\t    (is (= \"4\"\n29\t           (xl/call [:typescript \"globalThis.ts_fn = (x, y) => x + y;\"]\n30\t                    [\"ts_fn\"]\n31\t                    [:php \"<?php echo ts_fn(1.5, 2.5);\"]))))\n32\t  (testing \"the PHP caller sees the result as an ordinary value\"\n33\t    (is (= \"yes\"\n34\t           (xl/call [:typescript \"globalThis.ts_fn = (x, y) => x + y;\"]\n35\t                    [\"ts_fn\"]\n36\t                    [:php \"<?php echo ts_fn(1.5, 2.5) == 4 ? 'yes' : 'no';\"])))))\n37\t\n38\t\n39\t(deftest php-closure-called-from-ts-test\n40\t  (testing \"TS stores and calls the same PHP function cell it received\"\n41\t    (is (= {:js/out [\"true 5\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n42\t           (xl/call [:php \"<?php $phpfn = fn($a, $b) => $a + $b;\"]\n43\t                    [\"phpfn\"]\n44\t                    [:typescript\n45\t                     \"const stored = phpfn; console.log(stored === phpfn, stored(2, 3));\"])))))\n46\t\n47\t\n48\t(deftest limits-test\n49\t  (testing \"a PHP array returned to TS is an opaque handle, usable in PHP\"\n50\t    (let [src \"<?php $phpfn = fn($a = 7) => $a === 7 ? [1, 2, 3] : count($a);\"]\n51\t      ;; the PHP int `count` returns reaches TS as an integer (`3n`), not a\n52\t      ;; JS number: the two preludes keep their own number kinds\n53\t      (is (= {:js/out [\"3n\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n54\t             (xl/call [:php src]\n55\t                      [\"phpfn\"]\n56\t                      [:typescript \"const h = phpfn(); console.log(phpfn(h));\"])))))\n57\t  (testing \"PHP null is neither JS null nor undefined\"\n58\t    (let [src \"<?php $phpfn = fn() => null;\"]\n59\t      (is (= {:js/out [\"false false\"], :js/uncaught nil}\n60\t             (xl/call [:php src]\n61\t                      [\"phpfn\"]\n62\t                      [:typescript\n63\t                       \"const n = phpfn(); console.log(n === null, n === undefined);\"]))))))"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_yNgMflRE9xXz0zVSfk1d5CAu","content":"1\t(ns yang.call.conformance\n2\t  \"The cross-language calling gates' shared composition (docs/design/\n3\t   yang.antlr.md section 8.10.11): a donor program's named export reaches a\n4\t   caller program by explicit published-export composition only.\n5\t\n6\t   A donor is real source of any admitted frontend, lowered unmodified and\n7\t   published as an ordinary linker module whose one export, `body`, is the\n8\t   lowered unit. A caller task requires that module, runs its body under the\n9\t   donor runtime's own entry (`js/run-main`, `php/run-main`), reads each\n10\t   named export from the donor runtime's global namespace, and projects it\n11\t   into the caller runtime's namespace under the same name; then the caller\n12\t   source, lowered unmodified, runs under its own entry. The composition is\n13\t   a sequence of top-level nodes: no call node is rewritten, no foreign\n14\t   `:code` is extracted, no language-pair wrapper is inserted, and the\n15\t   projected value is the donor's own function cell (identity survives).\n16\t\n17\t   A callable value is task-local (a function is a cell, and cells are\n18\t   task-local, section 8.11), so the export is answered as a node evaluated\n19\t   in the caller's task, never as a host value carried between tasks.\n20\t   `export-program` answers the donor's export alone as the program's value.\n21\t\n22\t   Every program runs linked on the three vector VMs (`semantic`, `stack`,\n23\t   `register`) over the TypeScript linked harness's content store, where\n24\t   `yang.call` and `js` already live and `php` is published beside them.\n25\t   The AST walker is not a backend: its links are refused until L-b.\"\n26\t  (:require\n27\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n28\t    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\n29\t    [yang.core.names :as names]\n30\t    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n31\t    [yang.php.antlr.cst :as php-cst]\n32\t    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php-lower]\n33\t    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as php-h]\n34\t    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as php-prelude]\n35\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.cst :as ts-cst]\n36\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n37\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as ts-lower]\n38\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]\n39\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n40\t\n41\t\n42\t(def ^:private published-php\n43\t  \"`php` published once into `js`'s content store, pinning the same\n44\t   `yang.call` revision (as `source-call-test` publishes it).\"\n45\t  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\n46\t           (php-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n47\t                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\n48\t\n49\t\n50\t(defn- parse-ok\n51\t  \"The CST packet of `source` under `parse`, refused unless the parse is ok.\"\n52\t  [parse source]\n53\t  (let [pk (parse source)]\n54\t    (when-not (= :yang.cst/ok (:yang.cst/outcome pk))\n55\t      (throw (ex-info \"donor or caller source does not parse\"\n56\t                      {:source source, :packet (dissoc pk :yang.cst/nodes)})))\n57\t    pk))\n58\t\n59\t\n60\t(def frontends\n61\t  \"Each admitted frontend's profile, as data:\n62\t\n63\t   - `:runtime`, `:address`: the runtime module and its published address;\n64\t   - `:refusal`: the publication refusal key and reason of its modules;\n65\t   - `:parse`: source text to CST packet;\n66\t   - `:unit`: packet to the unmodified lowered unit, the function its\n67\t     `:run-main` entry takes;\n68\t   - `:read-export`: export name to the form reading the runtime's global\n69\t     namespace (JS `globalThis`, PHP `$GLOBALS`);\n70\t   - `:project`: name and a value form to the form binding the value where\n71\t     the runtime's source resolves a called name (a JS global, a PHP\n72\t     function);\n73\t   - `:render`: the `:run-main` value as test data.\"\n74\t  {:typescript\n75\t   {:runtime 'js,\n76\t    :address #(:address @h/published),\n77\t    :refusal [:yang.typescript.antlr/refusal :yang.typescript.antlr/undeclared-free],\n78\t    :parse #(parse-ok ts-cst/parse-source %),\n79\t    :unit #(names/canonicalize (ts-lower/lower-unit %)),\n80\t    :run-main 'js/run-main,\n81\t    :read-export (fn [export] (list 'js/global-get {:js/str export})),\n82\t    :project (fn [name value] (list 'js/define-global! name value)),\n83\t    :render render/output},\n84\t   :php\n85\t   {:runtime 'php,\n86\t    :address #(:address @published-php),\n87\t    :refusal [:yang.php/refusal :yang.php/undeclared-free],\n88\t    :parse #(parse-ok php-cst/parse-source %),\n89\t    :unit #(u/lam [] (php-lower/lower-module-body %)),\n90\t    :run-main 'php/run-main,\n91\t    :read-export (fn [export] (list 'php/global-peek export)),\n92\t    :project (fn [name value]\n93\t               (list 'php/declare-function! (str/lower-case name) value)),\n94\t    :render php-h/render}})\n95\t\n96\t\n97\t(defn- profile\n98\t  [frontend]\n99\t  (or (get frontends frontend)\n100\t      (throw (ex-info \"frontend not admitted\" {:frontend frontend}))))\n101\t\n102\t\n103\t(defn publish-donor!\n104\t  \"Publish the donor `source` of `frontend` as the module `module` (default\n105\t   `xlang.donor.<frontend>`), exporting `body`, its unmodified lowered unit.\n106\t   Answers `{:frontend :module :address :links}`.\"\n107\t  ([frontend source]\n108\t   (publish-donor! frontend source (symbol (str \"xlang.donor.\" (name frontend)))))\n109\t  ([frontend source module]\n110\t   (let [{:keys [runtime address refusal parse unit]} (profile frontend)\n111\t         [refusal-key reason] refusal\n112\t         spec (core-module/module-spec\n113\t                refusal-key reason (h/registry)\n114\t                {:name module,\n115\t                 :ast (core-module/module-tree\n116\t                        [(core-module/require-node runtime)\n117\t                         (u/def! 'body (unit (parse source)))]),\n118\t                 :exports '#{body},\n119\t                 :runtime-name runtime,\n120\t                 :runtime-address (address)})\n121\t         result (h/publish-guest-module! spec)]\n122\t     {:frontend frontend,\n123\t      :module module,\n124\t      :address (:address result),\n125\t      :links (:links result)})))\n126\t\n127\t\n128\t(defn- runtime-entry\n129\t  \"Require and initialize each distinct runtime of `frontend-keys`, once.\"\n130\t  [frontend-keys]\n131\t  (into [(core-module/require-node 'yang.call)]\n132\t        (mapcat (fn [runtime]\n133\t                  [(core-module/require-node runtime)\n134\t                   (u/sexp->uast (list (symbol (str runtime) \"init!\")))]))\n135\t        (distinct (map (comp :runtime profile) frontend-keys))))\n136\t\n137\t\n138\t(defn- donor-run\n139\t  \"The donor module required and its body run under its runtime's entry.\"\n140\t  [{:keys [frontend module]}]\n141\t  [(core-module/require-node module)\n142\t   (u/app (u/v (:run-main (profile frontend)))\n143\t          (u/v (symbol (str module) \"body\")))])\n144\t\n145\t\n146\t(defn export-program\n147\t  \"The program whose value is the donor's `export`, read from its runtime's\n148\t   global namespace after its body ran.\"\n149\t  [donor export]\n150\t  (let [{:keys [read-export]} (profile (:frontend donor))]\n151\t    (u/mark-tails\n152\t      (u/seq-nodes (concat (runtime-entry [(:frontend donor)])\n153\t                           (donor-run donor)\n154\t                           [(u/sexp->uast (read-export export))])))))\n155\t\n156\t\n157\t(defn compose\n158\t  \"The caller program: the donor's body run, each name of `exports` read\n159\t   from the donor runtime and projected into `caller-frontend`'s namespace\n160\t   under the same name, then `caller-source`, lowered unmodified, run under\n161\t   its runtime's entry. Its value is the caller entry's value.\"\n162\t  [donor exports caller-frontend caller-source]\n163\t  (let [{:keys [read-export]} (profile (:frontend donor))\n164\t        {:keys [project parse unit run-main]} (profile caller-frontend)]\n165\t    (u/mark-tails\n166\t      (u/seq-nodes\n167\t        (concat (runtime-entry [(:frontend donor) caller-frontend])\n168\t                (donor-run donor)\n169\t                (map (fn [export] (u/sexp->uast (project export (read-export export))))\n170\t                     exports)\n171\t                [(u/app (u/v run-main) (unit (parse caller-source)))])))))\n172\t\n173\t\n174\t(defn link-source\n175\t  \"The serving composition naming the runtimes and the donor module.\"\n176\t  [{:keys [module address]}]\n177\t  (h/source {'yang.call (:call-address @h/published),\n178\t             'js (:address @h/published),\n179\t             'php (:address @published-php),\n180\t             module address}))\n181\t\n182\t\n183\t(defn- modules\n184\t  \"The host registry, admitted by every runtime profile that checks it.\"\n185\t  []\n186\t  (php-prelude/admit (h/registry)))\n187\t\n188\t\n189\t(defn run-program\n190\t  \"`{backend value}` of `ast`, linked against `donor`, on each vector VM.\"\n191\t  [donor ast]\n192\t  (let [src (link-source donor)]\n193\t    (into (sorted-map)\n194\t          (map (fn [backend]\n195\t                 [backend\n196\t                  (vm/value (h/run-linked backend ast {:modules (modules),\n197\t                                                       :link-source src}))]))\n198\t          (keys h/backends))))\n199\t\n200\t\n201\t(defn agreed\n202\t  \"The one value every backend of `results` answered, else\n203\t   `{:disagreement results}`.\"\n204\t  [results]\n205\t  (let [vs (set (vals results))]\n206\t    (if (= 1 (count vs)) (first vs) {:disagreement results})))\n207\t\n208\t\n209\t(defn call\n210\t  \"Publish the donor `[frontend source]`, compose its `exports` into the\n211\t   caller `[frontend source]`, run it on each vector VM and answer the\n212\t   caller's rendered value when every backend agrees (else\n213\t   `{:disagreement {backend rendered}}`).\"\n214\t  [[donor-frontend donor-source] exports [caller-frontend caller-source]]\n215\t  (let [donor (publish-donor! donor-frontend donor-source)\n216\t        render (:render (profile caller-frontend))]\n217\t    (agreed (update-vals (run-program donor (compose donor exports caller-frontend\n218\t                                                     caller-source))\n219\t                         render))))"}
{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_5ytNFvaoZxX5PF8cLq95a5lc","content":"1\t(ns yang.typescript.antlr.source-call-test\n2\t  \"S11: real source calls through the shared convention (§8.10.11).\n3\t   The composition publishes the separately lowered PHP body, runs it, and\n4\t   projects its resolved functions into the JS global namespace. Neither\n5\t   frontend's call nodes or function bodies are rewritten.\"\n6\t  (:require\n7\t    [clojure.string :as str]\n8\t    [clojure.test :refer [deftest is testing]]\n9\t    [dao.test-slow :as slow]\n10\t    [yang.core.module :as core-module]\n11\t    [yang.core.uast :as u]\n12\t    [yang.php.antlr.lower :as php-lower]\n13\t    [yang.php.antlr.portable-harness :as php-h]\n14\t    [yang.php.antlr.prelude :as php-prelude]\n15\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.linked-harness :as h]\n16\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.lower :as lower]\n17\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.prelude :as prelude]\n18\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.prelude-parity-test :as parity]\n19\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.render :as render]\n20\t    [yang.typescript.antlr.source-call-fixtures :as fixtures]\n21\t    [yin.vm :as vm]))\n22\t\n23\t\n24\t(def ^:private published-php\n25\t  (delay (h/publish-guest-module!\n26\t           (php-prelude/module-spec (h/registry)\n27\t                                    (:call-address @h/published)))))\n28\t\n29\t\n30\t(defn- source-module\n31\t  \"An ordinary module exporting the unmodified lowered source body.\"\n32\t  [name packet]\n33\t  (core-module/module-spec\n34\t    :yang.typescript.antlr/refusal :yang.typescript.antlr/undeclared-free\n35\t    (h/registry)\n36\t    {:name name,\n37\t     :ast (core-module/module-tree\n38\t            [(core-module/require-node 'php)\n39\t             (u/def! 'body (u/lam [] (php-lower/lower-module-body packet)))]),\n40\t     :exports '#{body},\n41\t     :runtime-name 'php,\n42\t     :runtime-address (:address @published-php)}))\n43\t\n44\t\n45\t(defn- projection\n46\t  \"Namespace composition only: preserve each resolved function cell.\"\n47\t  [names]\n48\t  (u/sexp->uast\n49\t    (cons 'do\n50\t          (map (fn [name]\n51\t                 (list 'js/define-global! name (list 'php/resolve-fn name name)))\n52\t               names))))\n53\t\n54\t\n55\t(defn- check-source\n56\t  [{:keys [module php-form functions ts-form expected]}]\n57\t  (let [expected {:js/out (str/split-lines expected), :js/uncaught nil}\n58\t        php-packet (php-h/packet php-form)\n59\t        ts-packet (php-h/packet ts-form)\n60\t        project (projection functions)\n61\t        bundled (u/mark-tails\n62\t                  (u/seq-nodes [(php-lower/lower-packet php-packet)\n63\t                                prelude/uast project\n64\t                                (u/app (u/v 'js/run-main) (lower/lower-unit ts-packet))]))]\n65\t    (testing \"bundled source on every VM\"\n66\t      (doseq [[backend run] parity/runners]\n67\t        (is (= expected (render/output (run bundled))) (str backend))))\n68\t    (testing \"published PHP source and linked JS on each admitted VM\"\n69\t      (let [donor (h/publish-guest-module! (source-module module php-packet))\n70\t            source (h/source {'yang.call (:call-address @h/published),\n71\t                              'js (:address @h/published),\n72\t                              'php (:address @published-php),\n73\t                              module (:address donor)})\n74\t            ast (u/mark-tails\n75\t                  (u/seq-nodes\n76\t                    [(core-module/require-node module)\n77\t                     (u/sexp->uast '(php/init!))\n78\t                     (u/app (u/v 'php/run-main) (u/v (symbol (str module) \"body\")))\n79\t                     (core-module/require-node 'yang.call)\n80\t                     (core-module/require-node 'js)\n81\t                     (u/sexp->uast '(js/init!))\n82\t                     project\n83\t                     (lower/lower-packet ts-packet {:prelude :linked})]))]\n84\t        (is (some? (:address donor)))\n85\t        (doseq [backend (keys h/backends)]\n86\t          (is (= :ok (get-in donor [:links (case backend\n87\t                                             :semantic :yin.semantic/code\n88\t                                             :stack :yin.debruijn.code\n89\t                                             :register :yin.debruijn.register)\n90\t                                    :status]))\n91\t              (str backend \" source publication\"))\n92\t          (is (= expected\n93\t                 (render/output\n94\t                   (vm/value (h/run-linked backend ast {:link-source source}))))\n95\t              (str backend)))))))\n96\t\n97\t\n98\t(deftest ^:slow source-calls-php-function-test\n99\t  (slow/guard \"source-calls-php-function-test\" #(check-source fixtures/direct)))\n100\t\n101\t\n102\t(deftest ^:slow source-foreign-store-and-callback-test\n103\t  (slow/guard \"source-foreign-store-and-callback-test\" #(check-source fixtures/callback)))"}
