{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_EzrDkaevMY3WJWEIkQD3vYv4","content":"docs/design/yang.antlr.md-25-Proposed amendment, 2026-10-29: section 8.10 specifies the shared function\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-26-calling convention for ANTLR-based Yang frontends, replacing its earlier\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-27-interoperability placeholder. This is a design proposal, not an\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-28-implementation or conformance claim: the Python, TypeScript, and PHP\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-29-preludes still have different callable entry paths. The related amendments\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:30:in sections 8.1, 8.5.6, and 8.11 have the same status.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-31-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-32-Updated 2026-10-01 with the Architect rulings of 2026-09-30 and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-33-2026-10-01, each accepted by the owner. Later sections cite them by the\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-34-short names given here:\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-35-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-36-- the cell ruling; mob D1 to D10 (round 2); the mutable-objects ruling;\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-37-  the Python mappability ruling.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-38-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-39-They amend sections 8.1, 8.5, 9.3, 9.4, and 9.5, add sections 8.5.1 and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:40:8.11, and add cross-references from sections 8.6 and 8.9. Landed on\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-41-master since: captured continuations are invocable on all four VMs\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-42-(`8f9f90b0`); effects are an unforgeable host type and callee profiles\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-43-bound the effects they may raise (mob D4, `9a69e58f`); task-heap cells,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-44-slice 1 (`5e790683`); and the pure `data` host module (`yin.vm.data`,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-45-`fe8bce4a`).\n--\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-53-- the C3 integer design and the C3 cross-ruling.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-54-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-55-The two cross-rulings are the converged rulings of the architect pair\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-56-(gpt-6-astra and fable-5.1), to which the owner delegated decision\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-57-authority. Where a design and its cross-ruling differ, the converged\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:58:ruling governs. These rulings amend sections 8.5, 8.5.1, 8.11, 9.3, 11,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-59-and 12 and add sections 8.5.2 to 8.5.4. They build on Python phase C1\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-60-and on heap reclamation, both landed (`34c3986b`, `60b60898`). When\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-61-written, none of them had landed; each was recorded with its\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-62-implementation pending in the slices it names. The implementation\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-63-status above gives what has landed since.\n--\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-199-  catalog.)\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-200-- JavaScript is described as future work in the Yang documentation; no\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-201-  corresponding frontend was found in the inspected Yang source\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-202-  directory.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-203-- `yin.vm` (`src/cljc/yin/vm.cljc`) already defines the canonical row\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:204:  grammar, projection, reconstruction, validation, occurrence relations,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-205-  and requirement extraction.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-206-- `yin.vm.encoder` (`src/cljc/yin/vm/encoder.cljc`) already separates\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-207-  frontend maps from row output. Its forwarding path currently throws on\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-208-  unsuccessful appends; a general compiler pipeline needs explicit\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-209-  staging and outcome handling.\n--\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-227-1. **Universal AST maps** are the frontend's semantic representation and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-228-   the walker's reconstructed image.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-229-2. **Flat rows `[id tag & slots]`** are canonical code content exchanged\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-230-   across durable or remote compiler boundaries.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-231-3. **Datoms `[e a v t m]`** record naming, publication, provenance,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:232:   diagnostics, and optional derived EAV projections.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-233-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-234-Do not introduce a second authoritative AST schema in which each language\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-235-persists its own node attributes.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-236-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-237-The design text contains conflicting descriptions of map ASTs traveling\n--\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-741-sequences between chunks.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-742-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-743-Canonical spans use half-open offsets into the original source bytes.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-744-Host character offsets, code-point positions, UTF-16 indexes, and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-745-inclusive token end positions are converted at the boundary. Line and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:746:column values are presentation projections.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-747-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-748-Preserve original source and transformation maps for language\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-749-preprocessing, including Unicode escapes, indentation processing, or\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-750-mixed-code regions. Do not normalize line endings or Unicode text\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-751-silently.\n--\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1000-   walker's reconstructed image. Never hashed, stored, or shipped.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1001-2. **Canonical flat rows** `[id tag & slots]`: one row per node, content\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1002-   addressed by `dao.jing/segment-key` over the row body. What streams\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1003-   carry, what `dao.jing` stores, what names resolve to.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1004-3. **Datoms** `[e a v t m]`: naming, publication, provenance, diagnostics,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1005:   and optional regenerable EAV projections.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1006-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1007-There is no second authoritative AST. Lowering constructs only nodes\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1008-admitted by `yin.vm/semantic-bytecode-grammar`. Class, generator,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1009-prototype, pointer, and language-specific scope nodes are not added\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1010-merely for frontend convenience.\n--\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1028-[D :literal 2]\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1029-```\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1030-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1031-`A` through `D` are schematic addresses computed from row bodies.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1032-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1033:The encoder owns saturation, projection, and occurrence side tables.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1034-Frontends do not implement competing hash schemes.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1035-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1036-### 7.2 Existing integration points\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1037-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1038-Reuse:\n--\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1098-fingerprint of a compilation: two compilations with the same pinned\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1099-inputs produce the same record address and the same output root\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1100-addresses.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1101-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-1102-Content addresses occupy `v`, not `e`. The transactor owns persistent\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:1103:local IDs and transaction time. Optional AST datom projections remain\nResults truncated to 100 lines (total: 423). Use offset=100 to see more."}
