{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_NDow6ZVRmnR37KzR3g0samPp","content":"docs/design/yang.antlr.md-4007-There is no implication that current Python, PHP, TypeScript, or a host\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4008-target has completed this migration.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4009-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4010:#### 8.10.11 Acceptance gates\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4011-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4012-Execute real lowered source bodies, not only synthetic functions with\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4013-the expected slot. A harness may compose published exports and namespace\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4014-projections explicitly. It must not rewrite call nodes, extract foreign\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4015-`:code`, or insert test-local language-pair wrappers to make calls work.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4016-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4017-Required evidence:\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4018-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4019-- **Local semantics:** existing suites preserve argument order, defaults,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4020-  required/extra arguments, keyword errors, receivers, exceptions, and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4021-  supported reference/static behavior.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4022-- **Direct calls:** each implemented frontend calls every other\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4023-  conforming frontend through the same mechanism in both directions\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4024-  with compatible values. Derive the test matrix from admitted\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4025-  frontends; do not hard-code it into runtime dispatch.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4026-- **Higher-order calls:** pass, return, store, recurse, and call back\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4027-  through received functions. Assert identity and captures without\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4028-  replacement cells.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4029-- **Callable admission:** source data with an entry-spelled property\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4030-  remains data; profile-constructed descriptors are admitted. Exercise\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4031-  supported PHP string/array designators both under local resolution and\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4032-  explicit callable export, preserving required late lookup without\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4033-  foreign namespace guessing.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4034-- **Presence and binding:** distinguish missing from explicit\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4035-  null/None/undefined; retain duplicate keywords until binding; supply\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4036-  bound self once; evaluate receiver/spreads/defaults at source-defined\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4037-  times and counts.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4038-- **Dynamic callability:** where supported, an existing instance becomes\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4039-  eligible after its class gains a call method and ineligible after\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4040-  deletion. Calls whose arguments change this metadata observe the\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4041-  correct source-required lookup time without instance rewrapping.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4042-- **Opaque values:** round-trip foreign objects, functions, strings,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4043-  float64 content, and exact integers unchanged. Assert aliasing and no\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4044-  silent rounding/null conversion. Unsupported operations yield\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4045-  documented guest errors.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4046-- **References:** absent/incompatible writable-location profiles fail\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4047-  before reference acquisition and the body, with no reference-induced\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4048-  writeback. Source-required side effects from evaluating arguments still\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4049-  occur; rejection must not erase them. Compatible profiles prove\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4050-  mutation, aliasing, cleanup, and suspension behavior.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4051-- **Exceptions:** cover binding failures, arbitrary foreign thrown data,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4052-  catch-all/typed catches, unchanged rethrow, replacement in `finally`,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4053-  protocol-error rethrow, condition-shaped thrown maps, and A-to-B-to-A\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4054-  propagation. Assert original exception identity and cleanup order,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4055-  not only rendered text. Store/return a generated `ForeignException`,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4056-  finish its creating activation, then rethrow it from another activation\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4057-  and assert recovery of the original condition and payload identity.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4058-- **Context lifetime:** repeated success/raise/success, cross-runtime\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4059-  recursion, and stream suspension/resume restore handler/depth/frame\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4060-  state and perform arguments/cleanup exactly once. Entry boilerplate\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4061-  must not double-count source recursion or tracing activations.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4062-- **Publication/custody:** bundled/linked forms agree; two importing\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4063-  tasks have independent state. Existing gates still refuse foreign-task\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4064-  cells, forged refs, host functions, and inadmissible continuations.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4065-- **Portability:** execute portable packet-to-UAST fixtures on JVM,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4066-  Node, and Dart over the four VMs wherever existing contracts admit\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4067-  the program. JVM-only parsers may supply checked-in CST fixtures;\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4068-  parser availability is distinct from calling conformance.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4069-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4070-Report callable kinds, binding/value extensions, actual host/VM\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4071-coverage as an explicit host-by-VM matrix, refusals, and remaining gaps\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4072-per frontend revision. A scalar example or common UAST grammar alone\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4073-does not establish conformance.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4074-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md:4075:### 8.11 Mutable objects and collections over cells\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4076-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4077-This section records the mutable-objects ruling. A mutable guest object\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4078-is one cell holding one persistent value, and the object's identity is\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4079-the cell:\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4080-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4081-- The guest reference is the bare `:cell-ref`. The type tag and payload\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4082-  live inside the cell's content, so `type(x)` answers the same through\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4083-  every alias. The content is a tagged header plus payload, for example\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4084-  `{type-tag, items}` for a list or `{class-ref, attrs}` for an instance;\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4085-  the exact encoding belongs to each language's runtime profile.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4086-- Immutable guest values get no cell. Numbers, strings, tuples, `None`,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4087-  and the like are plain tagged persistent values.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4088-- A slot gets its own cell only when the language lets that slot itself\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4089-  be aliased. PHP reference slots are the case. Go interior pointers need\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4090-  no extra cell: they are a `(cell, path)` pair.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4091-- Classes are objects too. Class attributes are assignable, so a class\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4092-  is a cell, and an instance holds a ref to it.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4093-- A mutation is `cell/get`, then a pure update, then `cell/set!`.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4094-  Persistent structures make the copy a path copy, not a whole-value\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4095-  copy. No atomic update form is needed: a task switches only at park\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4096-  points, and the prelude evaluates operands before the get/set pair.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4097-  `cell/swap!` is rejected, because applying a guest closure inside\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4098-  effect handling would need continuation frames the engine does not\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4099-  build there.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4100-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4101-```text\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4102-+--------------------------------+-------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4103-| Option                         | Ruling            | Why                                                            |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4104-+================================+===================+================================================================+\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4105-| One cell per object,           | Adopt             | `assoc` and `conj` are path copies, so a mutation costs two    |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4106-| persistent value inside        |                   | effect dispatches plus one pure call regardless of size.       |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4107-+--------------------------------+-------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4108-| One cell per field or element  | Reject as default | A list of n elements means n allocations, n seals, and n heap  |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4109-|                                |                   | entries. Dicts with dynamic keys need a container anyway.      |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4110-+--------------------------------+-------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4111-| Host mutable objects           | Forbidden         | Violates \"no shared mutable state\" and the section 8.1 rule    |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4112-|                                |                   | that aliased guest objects share logical identity, not host    |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4113-|                                |                   | mutable objects.                                               |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4114-+--------------------------------+-------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4115-```\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4116-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4117-Aliasing and identity:\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4118-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4119-- Aliasing falls out. After `a = []; b = a; b.append(1)`, both variable\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4120-  cells hold the same ref, so both see the update.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4121-- Identity comparison is `=` on two refs, which is true exactly when they\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4122-  name the same cell, because a ref is data. It never touches host object\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4123-  identity, so it is portable across CLJ, CLJS, and CLJD. Python `is`, JS\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4124-  `===` on objects, and Java `==` on references all lower to it. This is\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4125-  an invariant: if refs later become host types (mob D7), `=` on refs must\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4126-  still mean same-cell, and refs must stay usable as map keys, on every\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4127-  host.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4128-- Guest value equality is prelude code. Python `==` on lists recurses\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4129-  through cells; it is never host `=` on a value containing refs, which\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4130-  would compare elements by identity.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4131-- `is` on immutable values is same type and value, confirmed per\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4132-  language profile (owner decision 1). Python's reference permits it. A\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4133-  Java profile cannot use it: boxed objects and `new String` require\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4134-  distinct identity, so a Java profile gives them cells. For Python,\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4135-  value means content identity, so floats compare by binary64 content\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4136-  (section 8.5.4).\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4137-- The ref itself is a valid host map key, so default instance hashing\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4138-  needs no id extraction.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4139-- A guest-visible `id()` is not stable across a lift, because cell ids are\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4140-  task-local and re-minted on lift. This is accepted and documented as a\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4141-  limitation (owner decision 2).\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4142-- Functions: two closures from one lambda with equal environments compare\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4143-  equal structurally, while JS and Python require them distinct and allow\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4144-  attributes on functions. Full fidelity wraps a function as an object in\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4145-  a cell. Section 8.10 adds the shared entry to that same identity object;\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4146-  crossing languages must not allocate a replacement wrapper.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4147-  Historical spike status: bare closures left `is` on functions unsupported.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4148-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4149-Value-semantics languages map as follows. PHP reference binding cannot be\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4150-a lexical rebinding of the name, since a continuation captured earlier\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4151-would still see the old binding; that is why the reference marker lives\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4152-in the variable's cell.\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4153-\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4154-```text\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4155-+--------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4156-| Language feature                     | Mapping                                                                    |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4157-+======================================+============================================================================+\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4158-| PHP array                            | Plain persistent value stored directly in the variable's cell. Assignment  |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4159-|                                      | copies in O(1); the observable-copy rule is free.                          |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4160-+--------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4161-| PHP object                           | Handle = cell ref.                                                         |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4162-+--------------------------------------+----------------------------------------------------------------------------+\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4163-| PHP `&$x`, `use (&$x)`, `f(&$x)`     | A variable cell holds either a value or a reference marker pointing at a   |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4164-|                                      | shared cell; reads dereference one level. `$b = &$a` moves `$a`'s content  |\ndocs/design/yang.antlr.md-4165-|                                      | into a fresh shared cell and sets both variables to the marker.            |"}
