{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_KxhhCu0dF2pgVTCUsNnm1cPm","content":"bin/collab-tools/README.md:4:[`docs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md`](../../docs/agents/roles/orchestrator.md) and\nbin/collab-tools/README.md:5:[`docs/agents/delegate-invocation-reference.md`](../../docs/agents/delegate-invocation-reference.md).\nbin/collab-tools/README.md:6:They hold no policy: roles, routing, and review rules stay in `docs/agents/`.\nbin/collab-tools/README.md:13:`Session-ID: <uuid>` line in the prompt header (generate and record it first); a resume passes the id as the\nbin/collab-tools/README.md:25:Host conventions: [`docs/agents/build-n-test.md`](../../docs/agents/build-n-test.md) (\"Remote agent\nbin/analyze-deps.clj:136:(defn generate-graph\nbin/analyze-deps.clj:142:      (println \"Error generating dependency graph:\")\nbin/analyze-deps.clj:150:  (generate-graph)\nbin/analyze-deps.clj:215:    (println \"\\nFor detailed guidance, see docs/agents/malleability.md\")))\nbin/collab-tools/dispatch.sh:5:# Without a resume id the prompt header must carry `Session-ID: <uuid>` (generate-and-record first)."}
