{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_hLW1zXqJMjKUfKs5S7yrIiGO","content":"1\t(ns ^{:clj-kondo/config '{:lint-as {yang.typescript.antlr.prelude/defquoted clojure.core/def}}}\n2\t yang.typescript.antlr.prelude\n3\t  \"The `js` runtime profile, written as Universal AST\n4\t   (docs/design/yang.typescript.md sections 3, 9, 10; the T1 plan's\n5\t   section 6). JavaScript semantics for operators, coercion, equality,\n6\t   strings, objects, functions and exceptions live here as guest code,\n7\t   not in Clojure: the lowering only emits applications of these names.\n8\t\n9\t   Value encoding:\n10\t     undefined, null  :js/undefined, :js/null (and the never guest-visible\n11\t                      :js/tdz of an uninitialized binding): never host nil\n12\t     boolean          host true / false\n13\t     number           float64 content (`data/float64`) at the producer, on\n14\t                      every host (JS cannot tell 2 from 2.0 as a bare\n15\t                      Number). Arithmetic unwraps with `data/float-value`,\n16\t                      computes on bare host doubles and rewraps with\n17\t                      `data/float64`. The prelude holds no integral float\n18\t                      literal: 1 is written (data/float64 1)\n19\t     bigint           the bare exact integer, through `integer/*`; a number\n20\t                      and a bigint are told apart by content equality with\n21\t                      the same value as float64 (`js/kind-of`)\n22\t     string           {:js/str s} when the code units are well-formed\n23\t                      UTF-16, {:js/units [u ...]} otherwise; `js/mk-str` is\n24\t                      the one normalizing door, so strict equality of\n25\t                      strings is host `=`\n26\t     object           a cell holding {:js/type :object :proto <ref|:js/null>\n27\t                      :props <om> :extensible? true}; the guest reference\n28\t                      is the cell ref, identity is `=` on refs\n29\t     function         a cell holding {:js/type :function :code\n30\t                      (fn [this args] ..) :yang.call/entry\n31\t                      (fn [invocation] ..) :this-mode :strict|:lexical\n32\t                      :name s :length n :props <om> :proto ref}\n33\t     property slot    {:value v :writable b :enumerable b :configurable b}\n34\t     own-key map      `om`: {:index {key slot} :ints [..sorted..] :strs\n35\t                      [..insertion..] :syms []}; guest-visible order is the\n36\t                      vectors, never a host map's\n37\t\n38\t   Calling convention: source calls are (js/call f this args), with `args`\n39\t   a vector built by `js/vconj`; `js/call` supplies one invocation record\n40\t   to the shared entry after structural eligibility. Foreign entries use"}
