{"role":"tool","tool_call_id":"tool_uGRAw59l2E2Y5j8AvXkrx11Q","content":"collab/yang-clojure/1793288816996-engineer-yang-slice9.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log-4-{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'pwd && git status --short && cat AGENTS.md && cat docs/design/datom.world.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793288816996-engineer-yang-slice9.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log-5-{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_1\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'pwd && git status --short && cat AGENTS.md && cat docs/design/datom.world.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld-yang-s9\\n?? collab/1793288816996-engineer-yang-slice9.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log\\n?? collab/1793288816996-engineer-yang-slice9.prompt.md\\n# ==============================================================================\\n# datom.world – Development Rules & Architectural Foundations\\n# ==============================================================================\\n\\nSee [`docs/design/datom.world.md`](./docs/design/datom.world.md) for master architecture, core philosophy, foundational axioms, non-negotiable invariants, code style, development workflow, and operational guides (testing, team roles, agent delegation, website formats).\\n---\\ndescription: Core philosophy, foundational axioms, invariants, primitives (tuples, streams, host boundaries), architectural commitments, design principles, code style, and development workflow for datom.world\\n---\\n\\n# DATOM.WORLD ARCHITECTURAL FOUNDATIONS & DEVELOPMENT RULES\\n\\n## Core Philosophy\\n\\nEverything is data.\\nInterpretation > abstraction.\\nExplicit causality > implicit assumptions.\\nRestrictions are a feature.\\n\\n### Foundational Axioms\\n\\n1. **Everything is a Stream**: Portable I/O and system data flow through append-only streams; hosts may also install explicit local functions that perform direct I/O.\\n2. **Interpretation Creates Semantics**: Data is syntax; semantics only emerge through interpretation (one truth, many perspectives).\\n   At system scale, a \\\"system\\\" is an emergent property of interpreters of\\n   pure data, not an object, service, or stored artifact. Find the\\n   interpreters and the data they share to find the system.\\n3. **Code and State are Datoms**: Code (Universal AST) and runtime exe[...truncated]\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793288816996-engineer-yang-slice9.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log-6-{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1793128583916-architect-yang-latte-gap-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793288816996-engineer-yang-slice9.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log-7-{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_2\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/collab/1793128583916-architect-yang-latte-gap-plan.gpt-6-astra.findings.md'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"Completed-Local: 2026-10-28 02:25:06 ICT\\n\\nThe recommended path is **reusable compiler corrections plus an explicit LaTTe portability layer**, verified against the original kernel running on Clojure. Compilation success alone is not a landing criterion. No files were edited.\\n\\nArchitectural decisions below are binding recommendations; helper names, file layout, and equivalent lowering implementations remain implementer choices.\\n\\n**Verified findings that change the plan**\\n\\n- **Ast-walker tail calls are iterative without consulting `:tail?`.** Both its stepped evaluator and hot loop enter a closure body with the application-evaluation frame removed. Pending enclosing computations remain. At 100 and 1,000 recursive iterations, measured maximum continuation depth stayed at **2**. Removing tail flags made no difference. See [walker application transitions](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc:303).\\n- **The semantic VM depends on correct tail flags.** Its maximum return-stack depth was **0** for the same programs; removing flags produced **102 frames at 100 iterations**. Both hot loops completed 10,000 iterations. Projection preserves the flag, analysis treats tail calls as terminators, and runtime avoids pushing a return frame. See [semantic invocation](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc:190).\\n- **Both lanes have Clojure truthiness:** only `nil` and `false` were falsy; `0`, `\\\"\\\"`, `[]`, `{}`, `#{}`, and `()` were truthy. However, [compile-if](/Users/sto/workspace/datomworld/src/cljc/yang/clojure.cljc:228) incorrectly turns an explicit `false` alternate into `nil`. This was reproduced.\\n-[...truncated]\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793288816996-engineer-yang-slice9.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log-8-{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg --files test/yang/latte_oracle test/yang | sort; cat docs/agents/build-n-test.md; cat deps.edn; sed -n '1,240p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793288816996-engineer-yang-slice9.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log:9:{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_3\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc \\\"rg --files test/yang/latte_oracle test/yang | sort; cat docs/agents/build-n-test.md; cat deps.edn; sed -n '1,240p' test/yang/latte_oracle_test.clj\\\"\",\"aggregated_output\":\"test/yang/antlr/conformance.cljc\\ntest/yang/antlr/packet_test.cljc\\ntest/yang/clojure/stream_eval_test.cljc\\ntest/yang/clojure_test.clj\\ntest/yang/core/claims_test.cljc\\ntest/yang/core/names_test.cljc\\ntest/yang/cross_lang_test.clj\\ntest/yang/frontend_test.cljc\\ntest/yang/latte_oracle/case_a