uncated]\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793288816996-engineer-yang-slice9.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log-19-{\"type\":\"item.started\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/latte-kernel/latte-kernel/86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279/src/latte_kernel/typing.cljc'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"\",\"exit_code\":null,\"status\":\"in_progress\"}}\ncollab/yang-clojure/1793288816996-engineer-yang-slice9.gpt-6.1-sol.stdout.log-20-{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_9\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/sto/.gitlibs/libs/latte-kernel/latte-kernel/86fca0d1d054af005cb37395eae04500d45e6279/src/latte_kernel/typing.cljc'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"(ns latte-kernel.typing\\n  (:require [clojure.set :as set]\\n            [latte-kernel.syntax :as stx]\\n            [latte-kernel.norm :as norm]\\n            [latte-kernel.defenv :as defenv]))\\n\\n;;{\\n;; # Type checking\\n;;\\n;; Type checking, and more precisely **type inference**, is the *heart* of a\\n;; proof assistant based on type theory.\\n;;\\n;; In this namespace all the type-checking rules are implemented by dedicated\\n;; functions.\\n;;}\\n\\n;;{\\n;; ## Type context\\n;;\\n;; We simply use a vector for the type context, which allows to\\n;; maintain the scoping rules at the price of some inefficiency\\n;; (fetching is O(n)).\\n;;}\\n\\n(defn ctx-fetch\\n  \\\"Look for variable named `x` in the type context `ctx`.\\n  Returns the associated type or `nil` if there is no such variable.\\\"\\n  [ctx x]\\n  ;; (println \\\"[ctx-fetch] ctx=\\\" ctx \\\"x=\\\" x)\\n  (if (seq ctx)\\n    (if (= (first (first ctx)) x)\\n      (second (first ctx))\\n      (recur (rest ctx) x))\\n    nil))\\n\\n(defn ctx-put\\n  \\\"Add variable `x` bound to type `t` in context `ctx`, potentially\\n  shadowing other variables with the same name.\\\"\\n  [ctx x t]\\n  (cons [x t] ctx))\\n\\n;;{\\n;; ## Synthesis rules\\n;;\\n;; All the type inference rules are given below.\\n;;\\n;;}\\n\\n(declare type-of-type\\n         type-of-var\\n         type-of-prod\\n         type-of-abs\\n         type-of-app\\n         type-of-ref\\n         type-of-ascribe)\\n\\n;;{\\n;; The following function is the main entry point for type inference.\\n;;}\\n\\n(declare unfold-implicit)\\n\\n(defn type-of-term\\n  \\\"Infer the type of term `t` in definitional environment `def-env`\\n  and type context `ctx`.\\n  The returned value is of th[...truncated]\n--\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-632-   - a repeated `ok` carrying `:dao.stream/value` but no `:dao.stream/cursor`\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-633-     must terminate by **throwing**, not spin (r4/P1-1);\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-634-   - a **conforming** `gap` — outcome plus its required `:dao.stream/cursor` —\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-635-     must hit the totality throw (F4). This is the only pin on S10 once §7\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-636-     deletes the gap test, and it is legitimate where a transport fixture is\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:637:     not: `conformance.cljc` forbids a *fixture inducing an excluded outcome\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-638-     on the transport*, not a double proving the consumer's own precondition\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-639-     check. Pair it with a `cursor-mismatch` case for the same reason.\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-640-3. **T19 and T20, in `schema_test`** — a `memory-log`-backed writer double\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-641-   answering `full` once then succeeding. Assert: after the failed\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-642-   `schema/transact!` the wrapper's schema and uniqueness state are identical\n--\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-829-\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-830-`publish-index-gap-local-stream-throws-before-emission` (`index_test`:375-392)\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-831-and the gap sub-case of `malformed-or-gapped-retained-history-throws`\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-832-(`transactor_test`:323-335) both build a capacity-bearing ring buffer, overflow\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-833-it, and assert a throw. Under D9 that fixture *is* the host-assembly defect the\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:834:contract names, and `conformance.cljc`'s exclusion principle is explicit:\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-835-\"Fixtures must never be required for excluded outcomes: a fixture inducing one\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-836-would contradict the exclusion it is meant to support.\" The exclusion is\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-837-discharged by the structural argument in `memory-log`'s docstring — one dense\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-838-vector from position 0, no expression that removes an element.\ncollab/dao-space/1788950282826-architect-space-transactor-v2-plan-r5.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-839-\n--\ncollab/general/adversarial-traces-not-policy.glm-5.3.findings.md-45-\"Carried onward … as data\" is true today of a return value, an `ex-data`, and a future medium alike; the carve-out is in the sentence; answers and values share the carrying duty without sharing a disposition. The *Host Boundaries* sentence is the right addition with the same disease in miniature: \"never what it means or what should happen\" would indict `dispatch-request`'s `:handler-error \"Handler failed\"` unless the happened/meant line is drawn — propose *\"says what was received and what happened, never what it means or what should be done about it.\"*\ncollab/general/adversarial-traces-not-policy.glm-5.3.findings.md-46-\ncollab/general/adversarial-traces-not-policy.glm-5.3.findings.md-47-## 7. Cost accounting: nearly complete; I checked the two candidates it might have missed\ncollab/general/adversarial-traces-not-policy.glm-5.3.findings.md-48-\ncollab/general/adversarial-traces-not-policy.glm-5.3.findings.md-49-- **`serving`** — needs no change, and the proposal's claim is verified: its status `case` ends in a default that closes the session (serving.cljc:317–330), so the two new terminal statuses flow through unhandled-by-name, which is the correct disposition of the *connection*.\ncollab/general/adversarial-traces-not-policy.glm-5.3.findings.md:50:- **`conformance.cljc`** — verified clean: no malformed-answer fixtures, no `transport-error` expectations; untouched.\ncollab/general/adversarial-traces-not-policy.glm-5.3.findings.md-51-- **The only other fold consumer is `rpc.cljc:125` itself** — counted.\ncollab/general/adversarial-traces-not-policy.glm-5.3.findings.md-52-- It is **six** code namespaces, not five (`runtime.v2` is listed in §6 but the framing counts five) — a slip, not an omission.\ncollab/general/adversarial-traces-not-policy.glm-5.3.findings.md-53-- The genuine misses are filed below: the descriptor enrichment, the docstring paragraph that does not \"stand,\" and the correction-of-`b2bf609` lineage.\ncollab/general/adversarial-traces-not-policy.glm-5.3.findings.md-54-\ncollab/general/adversarial-traces-not-policy.glm-5.3.findings.md-55-## Findings\n--\ncollab/core-datom/1789562719000-review-nil-fill-param-binding.gpt-6-astra.stdout.log-20-{\"type\":\"item.completed\",\"item\":{\"id\":\"item_8\",\"type\":\"command_execution\",\"command\":\"/bin/zsh -lc 'python3 .agents/skills/code-review-pr/scripts/pr_reviewer.py analyze --target working'\",\"aggregated_output\":\"# Code Review Summary for `working`\\n\\n## Executive Overview\\n- **Total Files Changed:** 7\\n- **Lines Added:** +164 | **Lines Deleted:** -48\\n- **Test-to-Source Additions Ratio:** 6.93 (104 test lines vs 15 source lines)\\n- **Overall Change Risk:** `MEDIUM`\\n\\n### Included Commits\\n- a450447 test(dao.space): prove free/bound variables are derivable by query\\n- c5cea20 fix(yin.vm): remove :global from the ast->semantic-bytecode grammar\\n- 5288448 docs(yin.vm): retire :global, derive free/bound variables by query\\n- 84f8eef feat(yin.vm): implement ast->semantic-bytecode map<->rows codec projection\\n- 33fdded docs(dao.jing): record canonical encoder contract and open items\\n\\n## Automated Scan Findings\\n✅ No critical security or code quality smells detected by automated scan.\\n\\n## File Churn & Risk Breakdown\\n| File Path | Category | +Add | -Del | Risk |\\n| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |\\n| `src/cljc/yin/vm/ast_walker.cljc` | Source Code | +6 | -3 | `Medium` |\\n| `src/cljc/yin/vm/engine.cljc` | Source Code | +8 | -0 | `Medium` |\\n| `src/cljc/yin/vm/semantic.cljc` | Source Code | +1 | -1 | `Medium` |\\n| `docs/agents/team.md` | Documentation | +45 | -44 | `Low` |\\n| `test/