dy {:type :variable, :name (quote y)}}, :operands [{:type :literal, :value 1}]}}, :operands [{:type :literal, :value :outer-y}]}))\\n  actual: (not (nil? :outer-y))\\n\\nERROR in (under-arity-zero-args-call-binds-param-to-nil-test) (observer.cljc:212)\\nCalling a closure with no arguments binds its declared param to\\n            nil (exercises apply-function's zero-operand path)\\nexpected: (nil? (compile-and-run {:type :application, :operator {:type :lambda, :params [(quote x)], :body {:type :variable, :name (quote x)}}, :operands []}))\\n  actual: clojure.[...truncated]\n--\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-28-\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-29-The creation specification is `{:dao.stream/type :dao.stream/memory-log}` with **no transport-owned keys**. There is deliberately no capacity key: capacity is the knob the contract just disowned for this purpose (`dao.stream.md:707-709`), and offering one invites the sizing mistake back in.\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-30-\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-31-## 2. The manifest\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-32-\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:33:Declared operations are `create!`, `descriptor`, `cursor`, `next`, `append!`, `close!`. **`attach!` is absent, not excluded** — the transport has no attach implementation, so there is no operation whose outcomes to declare. `validate-manifest` (`conformance.cljc:24`) requires only `:descriptor` plus the operations its declared surfaces license, so an absent `:attach!` key is valid. A host dispatch table supplies no `:dao.stream/attach` for this type and `host-dispatch-attach!` answers `:dao.stream/not-found` — the contract's own answer for a descriptor with nothing behind it (`dao.stream.md:233-239`).\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-34-\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-35-```clojure\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-36-(def memory-log-manifest\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-37-  {:dao.stream/type log/transport-type\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-38-   :surfaces #{:reader :writer :closable}\n--\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-128-\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-129-The manifest passes `validate-manifest` as written: `produces ∪ exclusions` equals `v2/operation-outcomes` per declared op, the sets are disjoint, every exclusion carries a non-empty reason.\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-130-\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-131-Three law blocks behave differently from the ring buffer's run:\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-132-\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:133:- `run-reader-laws` (`conformance.cljc:171`) mints `:oldest` on a fresh handle and reads it twice. Here `:oldest` is position 0 and stays there forever, so the block passes for a stronger reason than on the ring buffer, where the anchor tracks an advancing watermark.\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-134-- `run-induction-coverage` (`:112`) needs no `gap` inducer, since `gap` is excluded — the ring buffer's `gap` fixture (`ringbuffer_test.cljc:134-138`) has no counterpart and must not be reproduced by contrivance.\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-135-- `run-close-laws` (`:231`) closes the logical stream, not an attachment.\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-136-\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-137-**The abstract model needs no change.** `make-abstract-stream-model` (`:382`) already takes `capacity nil`, and its trim is guarded by `(and (:capacity state) …)` (`:481-485`). With no attachments, `visible-tail` is `:next-pos` and `retained-first` is 0 once anything is appended (`:next-pos`, also 0, when empty), so the `:oldest` expectation `(min (retained-first state) (visible-tail state inv))` (`:509`) is 0 at every state. That is the contract's \"a fresh `:oldest` *is* the origin\" already encoded in the model. Supply a `:cursor-projector` for this transport's cursor keys and `capacity nil`; nothing else.\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-138-\n--\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-147-> A `:dao.stream/oldest` cursor minted at any time is at the origin, and an origin cursor kept from before the first append replays every value in order without a `gap`.\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-148-\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-149-Add both, in two places:\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-150-\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-151-1. **In `memory_log_test.cljc`** — a `complete-retention` deftest: mint an origin cursor, append N = 1000 values (past any plausible window), replay the kept cursor asserting every read is `ok`, values arrive in order, and no outcome is `gap`; then assert a freshly minted `:oldest` equals the origin cursor. This is `ringbuffer_test.cljc:23`'s `retention-and-gaps` inverted, and a ring buffer fails it.\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md:152:2. **In `conformance.cljc`** — a `run-retention-laws` block, ~25 lines, run from `run-conformance-suite` only when the manifest declares `:retention :complete`. It checks (a) that `:next` excludes `:dao.stream/gap` — the two declarations may not disagree — and (b) the origin property above over `:handle-factory`. This makes the declaration mean something for the next complete-retention transport as well as this one, and it is falsifiable in this repo's existing style (`linearizability-oracle-rejects-an-invalid-history`, `:261`): bolt `:retention :complete` onto the ring buffer manifest in a local `let` and the block must fail.\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-153-\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-154-`:retention :complete` is a **manifest** declaration — configuration provenance, which the contract permits — not a predicate on a handle, which it forbids (`dao.stream.md:764-767`). If a reviewer judges (2) harness creep, (1) alone suffices and (2) drops without changing the transport.\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transport.claude-fable-5-1.findings.md-155-\ncollab/dao-stream/1788876999259-architect-v2-complete-retention-transpo