{"role":"assistant","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_9Tm6kJ1Qb7p6A4wdGYKZYSPG","function":{"name":"Write","arguments":"{\"path\":\"collab/orch-lane/1794160000000-engineer-xlang-s1.kimi-k3.1-pro.findings.md\",\"content\":\"# xlang slice 1 findings\\n\\nCompleted on `feat/xlang-matrix`.\\n\\n## What the muse partial work got right\\n\\n- The ordinary-module donor composition is the correct seam: source is parsed and lowered unmodified, the donor body runs under its own `run-main`, and only runtime namespace values are projected.\\n- The TypeScript linked harness supplies the right content store and three vector VM runners; `yang.call`, `js`, and the published `php` module compose without pair-specific wrappers.\\n- The rebuilt tests pin both directions, identity, PHP opaque arrays, PHP null, and backend agreement with five assertions in three tests.\\n\\n## What was wrong and changed\\n\\n- `php/global-peek` was the wrong export path for these cases. A PHP arrow function assigned to `$phpfn` is a PersistentArrayMap Closure descriptor, not the inner function cell. TypeScript can reject that descriptor as a non-function, and logging it can fall into number rendering. `php/callable-fn` intentionally preserves an already-eligible descriptor, so it does not solve the identity requirement.\\n- The PHP donors now use ordinary named functions and exports use `php/resolve-fn`, exactly as the existing `source-call-test` composition does. This preserves the donor's function cell identity without call-node rewriting, foreign `:code` extraction, or a language-pair wrapper.\\n- Each export is explicitly bound by a UAST `let` in the caller task before projection. No cell is carried as a host value between tasks.\\n- Documentation now names PHP's global function table rather than `$GLOBALS` for the export source.\\n\\n## Gates\\n\\n- Parser classes were initially absent; `clojure -M:antlr-gen` restored the standard generated sources before running the focused suite.\\n- `clojure -M:test -n yang.cross-lang-test`: **Ran 3 tests containing 5 assertions. 0 failures, 0 errors.**\\n- `clojure -M:kondo --lint test/yang/call/conformance.clj test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj`: **0 errors, 0 warnings.**\\n- `mise exec -- cljstyle check test/yang/call/conformance.clj test/yang/cross_lang_test.clj`: **passed.**\\n\\nNo slice-2 Python or Clojure legs were started.\\n\"}"}}]}
